@startuml interlock-check
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ArrowColor #3B4250
skinparam RoundCorner 8
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #EEF0FF
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #5B6CF0
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF6E5
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #3B4250
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam shadowing false
title How an interlock is checked (phyx3d interlock / check_interlock)

start
:Load the parts in their assembled positions;
:Pick the motion family from the type
(slide, twist, screw, snap, friction, custom);
:Build the insertion path
(from the spec's axis, depth, angle, pitch,
or the custom insert steps);
if (family is friction?) then (press fit)
  :Measure how deep the parts overlap per side;
  :Compare with 0.02 to 0.25 mm interference;
else (moves)
  :Fit in place: gap, touching,
  clamped or overlapping;
  :Sweep the removal path against the other parts;
  if (path blocked?) then (yes)
    if (hold = none?) then (yes)
      :Jams (reports where);
    else (no)
      :Held by the catch;
      :Engagement = catch height minus free play;
      :Compare with 0.2 mm (detent)
      or 0.6 mm (lock);
    endif
  else (clear)
    :Goes together;
  endif
  :Escape tests: 6 directions (and twists),
  free play in each;
  :Wrong ways: flip about X and Y, turn about Z,
  sweep the same path again;
endif
:Result: status, findings, fixes, data
and a picture;
stop
@enduml
